course: dictionary
lesson: 318
title: Flowers that are animals
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: An anemone is a flower with bright petals and a dark centre, but a sea anemone is an animal. The word sea is the clue. When you see sea in front of a word, ask whether the sentence is about the sea or a garden.
explain: «At low tide beadlet anemones pull in their tentacles and become jelly blobs to keep moist.» The words low tide, jelly and moist are clues. A jelly blob does not sound like a garden flower, so this must be the sea kind.
explain: «Clownfish live among the tentacles of sea anemones without getting stung.» The sentence tells you the anemone has tentacles that sting, and that the clownfish stays safe among them. Check your meaning by putting it in the sentence: a soft sea animal with stinging tentacles still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: An anemone is a flower with bright petals, often red, purple, pink or white, and a dark centre.
fact: A sea anemone is a soft sea animal that looks like a flower.
fact: Sea anemones stick to rocks and catch food with stinging tentacles.
fact: The name «anemone» comes from Greek and means «daughter of the wind».
fact: Clownfish live safely among sea anemone tentacles, and the two help each other.
exercise: «At low tide beadlet anemones pull in their tentacles and become jelly blobs.» What is a beadlet anemone? | A fish with a backbone | *A soft sea animal that looks like a flower | A tall garden flower | A type of wind
exercise: Grandma's garden has anemones with bright purple petals. Which kind is this? | A sea animal that sticks to rocks | A clownfish home | *A garden flower | A jellyfish
exercise: «Clownfish live among the tentacles of sea anemones without getting stung.» What do the tentacles of a sea anemone do? | Make bright petals | Hold up the sea | *Sting and catch food | Keep the tide out
test: «Clownfish lay eggs on a rock beside their anemone.» Which clue shows that the anemone is a sea animal? | Clownfish and eggs | Dark centre | *A rock beside the anemone | Bright petals
test: Priya says every anemone is a sea animal. Is she right? | *No, garden anemones are flowers | Yes, all anemones are sea animals | Yes, anemones are fish | No, anemones are jellyfish
exam: Which meaning fits «sea anemone» in «A sea anemone sticks to a rock and catches its food»? | A strong wind from the sea | *A soft sea animal that looks like a flower | A type of fish with fins | A bright red garden flower
